;. /procedure_extraction_flow
  ;@ /flow/definition procedure_extraction
  ;= Extract a procedure from retained work
    Bind capture to an own-record inspection cell for the retained attempt or
    investigation. Use its raw path, without /x. Bind sources to task and
    authoring evidence, and provider to the selected interactive provider.
    The task must name the Nenex action receiver, unused flow name, and selected
    steps or trace events. The result is a report linking an authored draft.
    Extraction does not publish the draft or replay arbitrary tool calls.

    ;@ /flow/input capture
    ;= Frozen native work selection
    ;@ /flow/input sources
    ;= Extraction task and native authoring guide
    ;@ /flow/input provider
    ;= Interactive provider

    ;@ /flow/step grounded ;/0x11/gov/flows/operations/library/captured_sources
    ;@ /flow/bind capture capture
    ;@ /flow/bind sources sources
    ;= Retain the exact selected native record

    ;@ /flow/step task ;/0x11/gov/flows/operations/library/surface_task
    ;@ /flow/bind pages document
    ;@ /flow/bind sources grounded
    ;= Prepare the authored extraction task

    ;@ /flow/step extracted ;/0x11/gov/flows/operations/interactive_requests
    ;@ /flow/bind tasks task
    ;@ /flow/bind provider provider
    ;= Use the existing extraction controls

    ;@ /flow/step report ;/0x11/gov/flows/operations/library/report_pages
    ;@ /flow/bind responses extracted
    ;= Read the validated report

    ;@ /flow/step pages ;/0x11/gov/flows/operations/evidence
    ;@ /flow/bind pages report
    ;@ /flow/bind sources grounded
    ;= Publish the report with compact provenance

    ;@ /flow/result pages
    ;= Extraction report

    ;@ /flow/page /
    ;@ /flow/uses native task authoring
    ;= Procedure extraction
      Read the selected native capture and the task. Identify whether this is
      a retained flow attempt or an investigation/model trace. Discover the
      Nenex page's declared authoring actions. Use Extract retained flow steps for
      retained executed flow steps, or Extract selected investigation events for investigation
      events. Use the actual control schema, not an invented argument encoding.
      Missing receiver, flow name or selection is a request for input through
      the existing work hole. Do not guess a new target or silently select every
      event. Before a trace extraction read its current sequence and selected
      entries; if they differ from the selected capture, request a deliberate
      re-selection. A frozen attempt remains valid historical evidence.
      Trace extraction runs on the owning page of that investigation. The
      existing controls create <new_name>_flow in the Nenex wiki; new_name is
      a definition name, not an arbitrary destination or relative child path.

      Native flow extraction retains the executed laws and their exact origins.
      Dependencies omitted from the selected steps become explicit inputs with
      frozen examples. Investigation extraction creates evidence inputs and an
      authoring hole; it is not executable replay. Preserve that distinction.
      Inspect the resulting source, input cells and extraction provenance.
      Explain which dependencies were exposed and which authoring decisions
      remain. Do not resolve the authoring hole or publish merely to finish this
      report. Those are separate deliberate operations.

      On resumption inspect prior action receipts and the destination before
      creating anything. Reuse the existing draft only when those receipts
      establish that this work created it. Never replace an occupied draft.
      Include the exact authored page, original work and receipt addresses in
      the report. Claim success only after inspecting the native result.
